Short:    HD-Installer for Stunt Track Racer Enhanced 2.0b
Author:   Codetapper/Action (codetapper@hotmail.com), ICQ: 26051687, Vesuri
Uploader: Codetapper/Action (codetapper@hotmail.com)
Version:  2.0b
Type:     game/patch
Requires: WHDLoad 17, 512k chip mem

Stunt Track Racer Enhanced 2.0b (27.11.2026)
Original install: Codetapper/Action. Version 2.0b: Vesuri.

This patch applies to "Stunt Track Racer" (c) 1989 Microplay.
Thanks to Chris Vella for the original.

REQUIREMENTS:
- Slave requires WHDLoad V17+.
- Game requires 0.5Mb chip mem (+0.4Mb other memory for preload option)
- Enhanced framerate requires a 68020 or later and 448Kb other memory

OPTIONS:
- CUSTOM3=1: Enhanced framerate, set in the installed icon. The game runs
  at 60 frames a second at its original speed, using the code of Stunt
  Track Racer Unleashed 1.1 by Vesuri. 0 or unset keeps the original frame
  rate. A 68000 or 68010 ignores it.
- CUSTOM1=1: start with infinite boost.

FEATURES:
- Full load from HD
- Loads and saves driver information to a separate file (which can be
  unpacked back onto a disk using DiskWiz or a similar utility to play
  from the disk version)
- Included save file has all 4 super division tracks ready for racing!
- Snoop problems fixed
- 2 access faults fixed
- Checksum removed
- RomIcon, NewIcon and GlowIcon (created by me!)
- Quit option (default key is '*' on keypad)
- Trainer (F6 to toggle infinite boost, Help to win the race)
- ButtonWait tooltype added
- International keyboard support (requires WHDLoad 12+)

This install was released because Keith's original JST install no longer
works on JST without disabling the MMU. There is also a checksum at the
start of the game which may cause problems later on in his version. The
disk image size is also half his version!

Greetings to Galahad/Fairlight for the turbo mode code and assistance
on several difficult installs, all Action members, my testing crew and 
the entire WHDLoad/JST team!


VERSION 2.0b (27-Nov-2026) done by Vesuri
- Enhanced framerate (CUSTOM3=1) on 68020 and later, set in the installed
  icon: 60 frames a second at the original game speed
- CUSTOM1=1 starts with infinite boost
- Trainer key moved from F1 to F6, since the game redefines keys with F1
- Turbo mode (F2) removed: the enhanced framerate replaces it

Codetapper/Action (06-Oct-2000)
Vesuri (27-Nov-2026)


